WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.100
And again, there are multiple ways

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.110
to approach this,

3
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.180
but I think one way that's very useful

4
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.620
is to focus on what I call

5
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.770
the decisive moment.

6
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.940
So for example, there are a couple

7
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.690
of decisive moments throughout my day.

8
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.450
Like at 5:15 PM,

9
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.560
my wife comes home from work

10
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.330
and either we change into our workout clothes

11
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.000
or we sit on the couch

12
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.300
and, you know, turn on reruns of The Office

13
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.270
or Netflix or something and order takeout.

14
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.500
And it's really the moment

15
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.660
of changing into our workout clothes

16
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.450
that determines what happens the next two hours.

17
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:35.910
If we do that one thing,

18
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.710
then we're gonna get in the car,

19
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:38.760
we'll drive to the gym,

20
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.660
we'll get under the bar,

21
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.430
we'll do the workout,

22
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.300
like the next two hours

23
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.050
are kind of already pre-decided if we change.

24
00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.720
So it's really mastering the habit of working out

25
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:48.980
is really about mastering

26
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.790
that first little decisive moment.

27
00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.760
And there's a similar moment in the morning

28
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.900
where I sit down

29
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.060
and either I open up Evernote

30
00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.580
and start working on the next article

31
00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:59.220
that I'm gonna write

32
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.120
or I go to ESPN

33
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.290
and check on the latest sports news or whatever.

34
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.700
And it's really about like

35
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.500
what I do in those first 60 seconds

36
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.960
that determines what the next like

37
00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.730
40 minutes are gonna look like.

38
00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.210
So I think for most people,

39
00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.260
there are maybe five or 10 decisive moments

40
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.360
like that throughout the day,

41
00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.000
little like forks in the road

42
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.720
that these inflection points

43
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.020
that determine how you're gonna spend

44
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.010
the next chunk of time.

45
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.920
And if you're trying to figure out

46
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.130
where should I focus first,

47
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:28.290
I would say focus on those decisive moments,

48
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.440
try to figure out like

49
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.740
what's the habit that I'm trying to change

50
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.340
and what is the decisive moment that precedes that,

51
00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.400
that determines what that block of time

52
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.310
is gonna look like.

53
00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.460
And what you come to realize

54
00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.920
is that there isn't actually that much

55
00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.200
that you need to change,

56
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.260
you're really focused on like

57
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.270
the first two minutes of the behavior.
